tion of families $(\\mathcal{F}_{1}, \\mathcal{F}_{2} , \\cdots , \\mathcal{F}_{k}) \\in \\mathcal{P}([n])^k$ is cross-Sperner if there is no pair $i \\not= j$ for which some $F_i \\in \\mathcal{F}_i$ is comparable to some $F_j \\in \\mathcal{F}_j$. Two natural measures of the `size' of such a family are the sum $\\sum_{i = 1}^k |\\mathcal{F}_i|$ and the product $\\prod_{i = 1}^k |\\mathcal{F}_i|$. We prove new upper and lower bounds on both of these measures for general $n$ and $k \\ge 2$ which improve considerably on the previous best bounds. In particular, we construct a rich family of counterexamples to a conjecture of Gerbner, Lemons, Palmer, Patk\\'{o}s, and Sz\\'{e}csi from 2011.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nOn Saturated k-Sperner Systems (https://people.maths.ox.ac.uk/scott/Papers/saturatedsperner.pdf)\nciteturn1search16 [wordlim: 200] Published: 6 months ago; Palmer, P´alv¨olgyi and Patk´os [11]. ... Conjecture 1 (Gerbner et al. ... Gerbner et al. [11] observed that their conjecture is true for k = 1, 2, 3.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nLucas Picasarri-Arrieta (https://lucaspicasarri.github.io/)\nciteturn1search5 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; # Lucas Picasarri-Arrieta ... As of August 2024, I am a postdoctoral researcher at the National Institute of Informatics (NII) in Tokyo working with Ken-ichi Kawarabayashi. ...   * On the list version of a conjecture of Erdős and Neumann-Lara\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nGeneralizations of the Tree Packing Conjecture (https://arxiv.org/abs/1104.0642)\nciteturn1academia17 [wordlim: 200] Published: 15.6 years ago; Authors: Dániel Gerbner, Balázs Keszegh, Cory Palmer ... The Gy\\'arf\\'as tree packing conjecture asserts that any set of trees with $2,3, ..., k$ vertices has an (edge-disjoint) packing into the complete graph on $k$ vertices.\n----------